{
    "word": "selfsame",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "026ffe04-a8e4-3824-8102-3d4fa014fdb8",
                "word": "selfsame",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                        "entry_id": "026ffe04-a8e4-3824-8102-3d4fa014fdb8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chiefly preceded by the: precisely the same; the very same; the same not only in being similar but in being identical."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ffc739b-74c7-4ad0-bc1b-d4ea77191856",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "For both of you are Birds of ſelfe-ſame Feather."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c199b252-1d7e-4a45-b1b9-e3bb389cf0d7",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "In my ſchoole dayes, vvhen I had loſt one ſhaft [i.e., arrow], / I ſhot his fellovv of the ſelfe-ſame flight / The ſelfe-ſame vvay, vvith more aduiſed vvatch / To finde the other foorth, and by aduentring both, / I oft found both. I vrge this child-hoode proofe, / Becauſe vvhat follovves, is pure innocence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a3558c5-52af-4538-889a-3928eb148399",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "He and his Horse, were of a piece. / One Spirit did inform them both, / The self-same Vigor, Fury, Wroth: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "701da24f-c266-4ef4-97ba-86a8f3b4f099",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "He trod the very ſelf-ſame ground you tread, / And victory refuted all he ſaid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f86f558-a6a9-4773-aed5-99f838f47b1f",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "Mine be the strength of spirit fierce and free, / Like some broad river rushing down alone, / With the selfsame impulse wherewith he was thrown / From his loud fount upon the echoing lea:— […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d47f060-19ed-4031-9b59-5f32a3bfa496",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "And Quack and Dupe, as we must ever keep in mind, are upper-side and under of the self-same substance; convertible personages: turn up your dupe into the proper fostering element, and he himself can become a quack; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c229fcf-11be-4c5f-843a-9b925135e50c",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "But in [Isaac] Newton, science was as easy as breathing; he used the same wit to weigh the moon that he used to buckle his shoes; and all his life was simple, wise, and majestic. So it was in Archimedes,—always self-same, like the sky."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15c9bdf6-fee3-48b2-b1cc-5eecbe6b5c20",
                                "sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                                "text": "[T]hrough my police issue 200 × 6000 macroscopic laser-prism binoculars I could see he was the same guy who had just bopped the doorman in the head. […] But you can imagine my surprise when I angled said state-of-the-art bins to the street, watched the long black car as it rolled up and saw the self-same guy step out of it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5497c7f3-d71c-4e79-96e8-084c1d8d3d6b",
                        "source_entry_id": "026ffe04-a8e4-3824-8102-3d4fa014fdb8",
                        "source_sense_id": "52423784-8535-3294-80c2-3cde08df65fc",
                        "source_sense_description": "precisely the same",
